  "prompt": "A charming midnight-purple miniature wizard hat with a broad square brim and a tall taper made from three or four stacked, progressively smaller cuboids, ending in a small tip. Paint a few tiny warm-gold stars on the front and side faces. Clearly reads as a wizard hat at tiny scale. No floating stars or particles. This is an equippable hat for tiny real-animal pets in vanilla Minecraft. Create the original hat ONLY, without a pet, stand, background or text. Fit all geometry within x=2..14, z=2..14, y=0..14, centred horizontally at x=z=8, flat wearable underside exactly y=0, facing negative Z. Use 4-16 purposeful unrotated axis-aligned cuboids, not voxels or smooth curves. Single compact shared painted cube-net atlas, one texel per model unit; explicit integer uvSize for any fractional geometry. No bones or animation. Connected robust forms, no z-fighting. Distinct Minecraft-style inventory silhouette. This will be uniformly scaled to each animal head with the bottom resting on its forehead; do not model straps, hair, ears or a head.",
